/**
 * TolerantSqlCommenter — a no-op qb SQL commenter whose `datasource` argument accepts ANY type.
 *
 * qb 13.x declares `appendSqlComments( required string sql, string datasource, ... )`. cbqManager
 * binds managed Connections to ON-THE-FLY datasource STRUCTS (ADR-0005: runtime datasources from
 * the encrypted registry, not pre-registered names), so the stock commenters reject the struct with
 * "argument [datasource] ... does not match the declared type of [string]" and every tool query
 * 500s. This variant relaxes the type and returns the SQL unchanged, letting struct-bound qb queries
 * run. Used only for `forConnection()`; the own store keeps qb's default commenter (it passes a name).
 */
@singleton
class {

	string function appendSqlComments( required string sql, any datasource, array bindings = [] ){
		return arguments.sql;
	}

}
